% Float operands/results cross the harness as integer bits, so tests check
% payloads and -0 rather than C's numeric equality (or printf's formatting).
% Arithmetic runs use parameters to prevent constant folding from
% replacing the SSE2 operation whose NaN operand order is being tested.
